markdown <<MARKDOWN
#### Let’s hear from Sal Khan, the creater of Khan Academy, and Hadi Partovi, the founder of Code.org, on what AI is and its recent impacts.

<br>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">A Note on Vocabulary</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:20px;">
    <p>

#### We'll dive into all the vocabulary around AI in the next module, but here's a quick refresher of some key terms.

>* #### **Artificial Intelligence (AI):** Teaching computers to think and make decisions like humans do.
>* #### **Large Language Models (LLMs):** Huge computer programs that are really good at understanding and generating human-like text based on what they've learned from a vast amount of written material. The technology behind ChatGPT.
>* #### **ChatGPT:** A smart chat program that can write and chat about almost anything by using what it's learned from a lot of books, websites, and other texts.
</p></div>
</details>

<details style="background-color: #ececec; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px;">
    <summary style="font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: bold;">📝 Key Points from the Video</summary>
<div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-left: 20px; margin-right: 20px; padding-bottom:20px;">
    <p>

* #### Recent advances like ChatGPT enable AI to generate creative content and ideas, expanding beyond pattern matching.
* #### Recent technology progress marked a shift from novelty to practical utility in education, with AI now able to understand and generate meaningful content.
* #### Generative AI can automate many educational tasks, potentially transforming the role of teachers and students.
* #### AI's evolving capability to act as a tutor or teaching assistant highlights its transformative potential in education.

</p></div>
</details>

<br>


MARKDOWN
